hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27836","Isma'il Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrated to us, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating to my father, he said: Marwan mentioned to me touching the private part, and I said: There is no ablution in it. So he said: Busrah bint Safwan narrates concerning it. So he sent a messenger to her, and the messenger mentioned that she narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"27837","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that he heard it from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr while he was with his father narrating that Marwan informed him, from Busrah bint Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution. He said: So he sent a messenger to her while I was present, and she said: Yes. So he came from her with that."
"27838","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me that Busrah bint Safwan informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever touches his private part, let him not pray until he performs ablution. Abdullah said: And I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm al-Ansari informed me that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: Marwan mentioned during his governorship over Madinah that ablution is due for touching the private part when a man reaches it with his hand, so I objected to him and said: There is no ablution upon whoever touches it. So Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention what ablution is due for. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And ablution is due for touching the private part. Urwah said: I kept disputing with Marwan until he called a man from his guard and sent him to Busrah asking her about what she narrated of that, so Busrah sent to him the like of what Marwan had narrated to me from her."
